      <activity id="05c6df7a-bfb2-533a-aef5-122da0a30b86" activityNameId="70214016-d849-57f0-aa7a-e60140c88b50" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Window frame, wood, opaquely painted, U=1.2 W/m2K, wall opening, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Window frame, wood, opaquely painted, U=1.2 W/m2K, wall opening, at plant
The measures of the window are 1.75m (width) x 1.3m (height). The wall opening is 1.8 m2 (assumption width of frame 0.12m, 2/3 of frame are behind the wall opening). 1m2 (wall opening) of wooden window frame weighs  21.2kg. The bill of materials is based on data from 3 window producers.;
UUID: 33f77673-a98f-33e8-9dba-3c22917516f2
Included are the materials used in a wooden window frame (with surface treatment). Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 window manufacturers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_33f77673-a98f-33e8-9dba-3c22917516f2.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
